course: dictionary
lesson: 7664
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and prop is one of them. You can be a noun or a verb. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because those are its context. «The props table holds things actors need» is about objects in a play, but «prop the door open» is about holding something up.
explain: Look at the clues. «They lift him into the car and prop him up with soft cushions» uses prop as a verb: the cushions are there to hold him up so he does not fall. In «Meerkats stand up tall on their back legs, using the tail as a prop», a prop is something that supports the meerkat.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. If «prop up» still makes sense when you put in «support», you have the right meaning. A dictionary can tell you the other meanings, such as the rugby player or the informal word for a propeller.
fact: «Prop» can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: A prop is an object used by actors in a play or film, like a sword, a crown or a cup.
fact: As a verb, «prop» means to support something so it doesn't fall, or to lean it against something.
fact: «Meerkats» use their tails as a prop when they stand up tall as lookouts for hawks and jackals.
fact: «Rainforest trees» grow buttress roots that prop them up like the walls of a tent.
exercise: «The props table holds things actors need for the school play.» In this sentence, what is a prop? | A tall tree in the rainforest | A rugby player in the front row | A stick used to hold a gate up | *An object used by actors in a play, like a sword or a crown
exercise: «Meerkats stand up tall on their back legs, using the tail as a prop.» What does prop mean here? | *Something that supports the meerkat so it stays up | A small animal that hides | A loud, sharp alarm call | A play on the stage
exercise: What word class is prop in «prop the door open»? | An adjective, because it describes | *A verb, because it is an action | A pronoun, because it replaces a name | A noun, because it names a thing
test: «They lift him into the car and prop him up with soft cushions.» Which meaning of prop fits here? | An informal name for a propeller | A player in the front row of a rugby scrum | *To support something so it doesn't fall | An object used in a play
test: «The rainforest tree has buttress roots that prop it up.» What does prop up mean? | *To hold up so it does not fall | To make a loud sound | To grow very tall quickly | To paint a picture on a wall
exam: In «rugby forwards such as a prop», what is a prop? | *A player in the front row of the scrum | A stage object used in a play | A stick that holds something up | A propeller on a boat
